          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Refractors vs Reflectors",
          "content": "Galileo used a refractor — light bent through lenses. Newton invented the reflector in 1668, using a curved mirror to focus light. Reflectors dominate today because mirrors can be made huge without chromatic aberration. The largest single-mirror telescope is 8.4 m; segmented mirrors push much larger (JWST: 18 hexagons forming 6.5 m; ELT: 798 hexagons forming 39 m).",
