"720\" y1=\"285\" x2=\"825\" y2=\"400\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"720\" y1=\"300\" x2=\"825\" y2=\"400\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"825\" cy=\"400\" r=\"15\" fill=\"#10b981\"/><text x=\"825\" y=\"500\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"white\" font-size=\"20\">Mirror bounces light</text><text x=\"825\" y=\"530\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"18\">Max ~40 m (segmented)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"650\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-size=\"24\" font-weight=\"bold\">Why mirrors win at scale</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"720\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"white\" font-size=\"22\">Lenses must be flawless throughout volume</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"760\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"white\" font-size=\"22\">Mirrors only need a perfect front surface</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"white\" font-size=\"22\">Big lenses sag under their own weight</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"22\">Coming soon: Extremely Large Telescope (2028)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"940\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-size=\"22\">39-meter mirror in Chile's Atacama Desert</text></svg>",
