          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Adaptive Optics: Beating the Atmosphere",
          "content": "Earth's turbulent atmosphere makes stars twinkle — and blurs telescope images. Adaptive optics uses a laser to create an artificial star in the upper atmosphere, measures how it wobbles, and deforms a flexible mirror 1000 times per second to cancel the blur. Modern ground telescopes with AO can match or beat Hubble's sharpness in the infrared.",
